      "id": "investment_discipline_premium_state_loading",
      "name": "Autoregressive Investment-Discipline Premium Loading",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "Construct a sector-relative investment-discipline exposure from low assetGrowth, low debtGrowth, and high operatingCashFlow relative to capex, with stale or invalid accounting observations masked. Form a daily factor-mimicking return from lagged exposures and close-to-close returns; multiply each current exposure by a volatility-normalized, slow EWMA/autoregressive forecast of that factor return, producing a cross-sectional signal that can attenuate or reverse when the factor premium regime changes.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "Firms with restrained asset expansion and internally funded investment tend to outperform aggressive expanders, but the short-run premium for this characteristic is regime-dependent rather than constant. Following the factor-timing logic in the source paper, estimate the recent realized return of a cross-sectional investment-discipline factor and use a heavily smoothed autoregressive state estimate to scale its stock-level exposures. The other side is investors and benchmarked managers persistently financing high-growth asset expansion or unwinding defensive quality exposures during risk-on episodes; the hypothesis fails if the investment-discipline factor's recent return contains no stable predictive information for its next-week payoff.",
